{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A maximum independent set (exact): of all the largest ones, the lexicographically least by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order; [] for the empty graph. Of two sets of one size, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":"’s rule, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on a loop-free graph this is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumClique()"},{"type":"text","text":" of the complement). A vertex with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop is never in it; parallel edges count once."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximumindependentset()"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumIndependentSet()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Covering"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE21maximumIndependentSetSay6VertexQzGyF","title":"maximumIndependentSet()","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumIndependentSet"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","symbolKind":"method","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1596","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"}},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumIndependentSet","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Looped vertices are removed and each connected component solved alone, since the rule","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"composes across components. A bipartite component costs O(m √n): a maximum matching","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Hopcroft–Karp), the alternating reach from its free vertices (König), and one greedy pass","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the perfectly matched core in index order along the Dulmage–Mendelsohn implications.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A complete component takes its least vertex. Any other component of c vertices is decided","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex by vertex in index order against a witness maximum set, shrunk between decisions by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rules that keep the least set (an isolated vertex is taken; so is a simplicial vertex, such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a leaf, less than all its neighbours), with pieces that turn bipartite or complete","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handed to the cases above. Each decision the witness cannot answer computes α of what is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"left of the vertex’s component by the degree-0, -1 and -2 reductions (taking a leaf,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"folding a degree-2 vertex) and then, on the kernel’s non-bipartite components, branch and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bound on bitset rows of the complement with a greedy-colouring bound (BBMC; San Segundo et","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"al. 2011). So trees with few extra edges, long paths and cycles cost O(c (c + m)) at worst","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and O(c + m) when the rules settle them; the search is exponential in the kernel’s size in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the worst case. Memory O(n + m + k² \/ 64) words for a kernel component of k vertices.","type":"text"}]}]}],"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","title":"Graph","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"type":"topic","title":"Covering","role":"collection","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/covering","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentat